course: dictionary
lesson: 9839
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. The word swing is a good example. «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height, so walk wide around swings.» Here a swing is a seat hanging on ropes that you sit on.
explain: «They swing their heads from side to side as they search.» Here swing is an action. It means to move from side to side. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something being done? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Swing can also mean a big change, as in mood swings. «Moving your legs and leaning at the right moments adds a little energy each swing.» In this sentence a swing is one full back-and-forth movement. Read the words around the word, and they will show you which meaning fits.
fact: To swing means to move backwards and forwards, or from side to side, while hanging from something.
fact: A swing is a seat hanging on ropes or chains that you sit on and move back and forth.
fact: A swing can also mean a big change, such as a swing in mood.
fact: In science, a swing is a pendulum: it goes back and forth in a steady rhythm.
fact: Useful phrases: swing back and forth, take a swing at, in full swing, mood swings.
exercise: «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height, so walk wide around swings.» What is a swing in this sentence? | *A seat hanging on ropes or chains | A tall tree with thick branches | A bat or racket used in sport | A big change in how you feel
exercise: «They swing their heads from side to side as they search.» What does swing mean here? | *To move from side to side | To fall asleep | To make a big change | To stop still and wait
exercise: Mia says her mood had a swing this morning. What does swing mean here? | A rope tied to a tree | To hit a ball with a bat | *A big change in how you feel | A seat in the playground
test: «A swing is fastest at the bottom and slowest at the top, and a roller coaster swaps height and speed the same way.» What does swing mean in this sentence? | *A pendulum, moving back and forth | To sit down on a playground seat | A big change in mood | To hit a ball with a racket
test: Jayden asks what «take a swing at» means. Which answer is right? | *To try to hit something | To change your mood suddenly | To stop moving completely | To sit on a seat and rock
exam: Ella reads «Young sunflowers swing back at night.» Which meaning of swing fits best? | To hit a ball with a bat | To hang from a rope and sit on it | *To move back, like turning around | A big change in mood
